# Code owners are asked to review changes to these paths. main does not
# require pull requests yet: the release workflow pushes manifest.json straight
# to main with GITHUB_TOKEN, which no ruleset can exempt. Once that push uses a
# deploy key, the "main: reviews and checks" ruleset can require code-owner
# review here too.
#
# They cover everything that runs with repository credentials or decides
# what ships: workflows and their scripts, the build and release config, and
# the files users install from. Everything else merges on green CI.
#
# Only org admins (and Dependabot) can push branches to this repository, so
# contributors open pull requests from a fork.

/.github/                @mondominator
*.csproj                 @mondominator
*.props                  @mondominator
*.targets                @mondominator
*.sln                    @mondominator
*.slnx                   @mondominator
global.json              @mondominator
nuget.config             @mondominator
NuGet.Config             @mondominator
/build.yaml              @mondominator
/meta.json               @mondominator
/manifest.json           @mondominator

# Agent and editor config runs on the maintainer's machine (hooks, commands,
# instructions), so it gets the same review as CI.
/CLAUDE.md               @mondominator
/AGENTS.md               @mondominator
/.claude/                @mondominator
/.codex/                 @mondominator
/.githooks/              @mondominator
/.vscode/                @mondominator
